<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/creatureportrait_twilightshammer_dragonegg_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Fire Mage Trinkets in Phase 1</span></h2>DPS trinkets tend to be very straightforward, as their damage is not affected by class damage buffs. Therefore, direct damage dealing trinkets should be used on cooldown as much as possible, unless aligned with specific boss damage taken increasing mechanics, and stat increasing trinkets should similarly either be used on cooldown or aligned with burst phases.<br/>
<br/>Additionally, it's relevant to note that as Phase 1 goes on, the Celestial Dungeons will become available soon after each raid releases - the Raid trinkets mentioned here are available through said Dungeons in their LFR versions, and are an upgrade over both of the Active Trinkets mentioned.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>Which type of trinket Mages use isn't very relevant, though passive trinkets are inherently easier to use due to the nature or not requiring actually thinking about it, making them better options for players who tend to forget and have low uptime on their item usages.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87175/essence-of-terror">
<img alt="Essence of Terror" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pvp_trinket.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Essence of Terror</span></a> is eventually your Best in Slot trinket, and should be the goal of any commited Mage (regardless of the specialization). It provides a ton of static Intellect, as well as a massive amount of Haste from its proc, meaning you can get extra casts during your major cooldowns.<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87065/light-of-the-cosmos">
<img alt="Light of the Cosmos" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_offhand_ulduarraid_d_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Light of the Cosmos</span></a> is the second Best in Slot trinket you'll ultimately use, this is has static Haste instead of main stat, but you can reforge a portion of it into Critical Strike. As for the proc itself, it's a low cooldown Intellect proc, allowing you to consistently get pretty good Ignites when it procs.<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79331/relic-of-yulon">
<img alt="Relic of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_dragon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Yu'lon</span></a> although not Best in Slot for the entire duration of the expansion for Fire Mage, it's used until you obtain Heroic <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87175/essence-of-terror">
<img alt="Essence of Terror" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pvp_trinket.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Essence of Terror</span></a>, making it a great investment for your performance.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81263/flashfrozen-resin-globule">
<img alt="Flashfrozen Resin Globule" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flashfrozen Resin Globule</span></a> provides some much needed Hit initially while still gearing up your character, allowing for more offensive secondary stats on the rest of your gear without worrying as much about getting to the Hit Cap - it's also very easy to obtain through basic Heroic Dungeons.<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89081/blossom-of-pure-snow">
<img alt="Blossom of Pure Snow" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_herbd.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blossom of Pure Snow</span></a> is available through the Shado-Pan reputation vendor, and is a great option if you haven't been able to obtain the <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81263/flashfrozen-resin-globule">
<img alt="Flashfrozen Resin Globule" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flashfrozen Resin Globule</span></a> and have plenty of Valor to spend, otherwise not much value in it since it performs about the same as the Heroic Dungeon option.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="reputation">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/achievement_faction_shadopan_assault.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reputation for Fire Mages in Phase 1</span></h2>Reputation gear can be very strong, but it can also be difficult to choose which factions to prioritize first.<br/>
<br/>As a Fire Mage, we recommend you prioritize <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/faction=1337/the-klaxxi">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Klaxxi</span></a> to get your hands on the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89062/klaxxi-lash-of-the-orator">
<img alt="Klaxxi Lash of the Orator" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_cloth_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Klaxxi Lash of the Orator</span></a> at Honored. Within the same reputation, if you manage to hit Exalted you are given a free ring - the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=90859/seal-of-the-lucid">
<img alt="Seal of the Lucid" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_147.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Seal of the Lucid</span></a> is a great option to use.<br/>
<br/>Additionally, Honored with <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/faction=1341/the-august-celestials">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The August Celestials</span></a> will give you access to the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=88742/sunspeakers-flared-gloves">
<img alt="Sunspeaker's Flared Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_cloth_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sunspeaker's Flared Gloves</span></a>, which perform slightly better than the Valor Shoulders.<br/>
<br/>Lastly, getting Honored with <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/faction=1269/golden-lotus">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Golden Lotus</span></a> will allow you to get the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89072/simple-harmonius-ring">
<img alt="Simple Harmonius Ring" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_147.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Simple Harmonius Ring</span></a> which you'll use for a long time unless you eventually get lucky with World Boss loot or contest a Spirit ring. Additionally, if you get Exalted with this same reputation, you then get access to a 389 item level necklace without need of Valor, and it's easily pre-raid best in slot, even above the Celestial Dungeon stuff.<div data-inserted-ad-group="1" style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; justify-content: center; align-items: center;">
