<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Fire Mages</span></h2>Every profession is relatively viable in Mists of Pandaria Classic, but engineering is always in somewhat of a class above due to the high quality of life tools it provides and safety net of nitro boosts. Tailoring also continues to be the best profession, especially due to its main ICD benefit being oftentimes re-applied with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=108978/alter-time">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_mage_altertime.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Alter Time</span></a>.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Fire Mages</h4>Engineering has plenty of quality of life tools, such as repair bots, access to the bank in raids, an extra slow fall option and such, but the two main factors that make it so good for PVE are:<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126731/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> is an on-demand big main stat cooldown which can then be prolonged with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=108978/alter-time">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_mage_altertime.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Alter Time</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55016/nitro-boosts">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a> allows the player to escape mechanics that one would otherwise not be able to get out of, as well as helping correct major mistakes in positioning with far less of a uptime loss.</div></li></ul>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="tailoring">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_tailoring.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tailoring for Fire Mages</h4>The main reason for getting tailoring is <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=125481/lightweave-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thread_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweave Embroidery</span></a>, this proc provides a fairly large amount of main stat, usually when most of your other cooldowns are also ongoing.<br/>As a bonus, you also get a far cheaper leg enchant with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=125496/masters-spellthread">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_astralrecalgroup.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Master's Spellthread</span></a>, since you don't have to buy the enchant from other players.<br/>Lastly, you can craft some BoE and BoP items that are useful at the start of the expansion. These aren't mandatory to obtain, but always nice to have the option to craft them.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted Gear for Fire Mages</span></h3>Although not very powerful when compared to other options which are available mid-way through Phase 1, there's a few crafted items that can help you get started in your gearing journey:<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82437/spelltwisters-grand-robe">
<img alt="Spelltwister's Grand Robe" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_robe_raidmage_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spelltwister's Grand Robe</span></a> although not equipped with the ideal secondary stats, its item level is higher than other items available initially. Also due to its higher item level, it helps you queue into Heroic and Celestial Dungeons faster.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82438/spelltwisters-gloves">
<img alt="Spelltwister's Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_raidmage_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spelltwister's Gloves</span></a> similarly to the former item, doesn't have great secondary stats, though the Hit is welcome since it allows you to more easily reach the Hit Cap. Same as with the same set chestpiece, it also increases your item level a fair bit early on - allowing you to queue into Heroic and Celestial Dungeons faster.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77533/lightweight-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Lightweight Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweight Retinal Armor</span></a> from Engineering allows you to pick the secondary stats you want using Tinker's Gears such as <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77545/rigid-tinkers-gear">
<img alt="Rigid Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rigid Tinker's Gear</span></a>, alongside its equally high item level considering the point in the game you can get it, makes for a must have crafted option early on.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79334/inscribed-jade-fan">
<img alt="Inscribed Jade Fan" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_offhand_1h_pandariatradeskill_c_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscribed Jade Fan</span></a> comes from Inscription, but you can buy it from other players or through the auction house, although not a great item by itself, it allows you to equip more powerful Main Hand Weapons as opposed to the Staves you might have currently.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79331/relic-of-yulon">
<img alt="Relic of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_dragon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Yu'lon</span></a> is an extremely powerful trinket that's also obtainable as soon as you hit max level, as Fire you'll use it until you obtain the Heroic version of the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87175/essence-of-terror">
<img alt="Essence of Terror" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pvp_trinket.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Essence of Terror</span></a> (from the third raid in Phase 1) making it by far the highest priority in terms of gold investment for your character.</div></li></ul>
